course: dictionary
lesson: 8628
title: Scruffy: untidy, but not always bad
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Scruffy means untidy, a bit dirty or worn out, or with messy, rough fur. You can use it for a person, clothes, a place or an animal. Read the words around it to find out which sense is meant. «A vulture lands last, bald and scruffy, but it is one of nature's cleaners» tells you the vulture looks untidy, but the word «cleaners» shows that looking scruffy does not make it bad.
explain: Jake's dog Diesel is «huge and scruffy and everyone crosses the road». The clue is in the second half of the sentence: «with Jake he's a big softie who sleeps on his feet». Scruffy can describe how something looks at first, even when it is kind underneath. Ask yourself: does the sentence say how the thing looks, or how it behaves?
fact: Scruffy means untidy, and a bit dirty or worn out.
fact: Scruffy can describe a person, clothes, a place, or an animal's messy, rough fur.
fact: The forms are scruffy, scruffier, and scruffiest, as in «a scruffier coat» and «the scruffiest dog in the park».
fact: «Scruffy clothes» means clothes that look untidy or worn out.
fact: A scruffy animal is often lovable, as in «a scruffy little dog».
exercise: «On the way home from school a scruffy street dog starts trotting behind you.» What does scruffy mean here? | *Untidy, with messy rough fur | Smart and well brushed | Brand new and shiny | Very fast and noisy
exercise: «Jake's dog Diesel is huge and scruffy and everyone crosses the road.» Why might people cross the road? | He is very small | *They think he looks untidy and rough | He is sleeping in the road | They want to say hello to him
exercise: Your teacher says, «Your uniform looks scruffy.» What should you do? | Wear it inside out to school | Ask for a different school | Take the whole uniform off | *Tuck your shirt in
test: «Once a year penguins moult all their feathers; they cannot swim or eat then, so they fatten up beforehand and look scruffy.» Why do the penguins look scruffy? | They are losing their old feathers | *They are losing their old feathers, so they look untidy | They have just won a race | They have had a long bath
test: What does scruffy mean in «scruffy clothes»? | Wet from the rain | Brand new and shiny | Very expensive and smart | *Untidy and a bit worn out
exam: Which word is the best synonym for scruffy when you describe a dog's fur? | *Messy | Silky | Tidy | Shiny
